{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508084-by-my-name-homebrew-pledgecraft","id":1508084,"title":"By My Name [Homebrew Pledgecraft]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-11T16:35:48-07:00","id":1508084,"title":"By My Name [Homebrew Pledgecraft]","content":"Fresh off my second read of Kith and Kin, and I think the more laid out possibilities for Oaths definitely help a lot - more agency to the players, more flesh on the world's skeleton for the ST.<br /> <br /> Don't hesitate to sound off on these ones, and to post your own ! <hr /><br /> <b>Oath of Silence</b><br /> The changelings agree to do their best to cover up an inconvenient or dangerous fact.<br /> <br /> Terms: \u201cIn my chest, I bury the embers of truth, lest they spark a fire that would engulf us all. I swear to speak no words but those we have convened, and to keep all dissenting clues from ever surfacing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Beat: The changeling resorts to violent or desperate measures to prevent the deception from unraveling.<br /> <br /> Willpower: The changeling manages to twist evidence as corroborating of the made-up tale.<br /> <br /> Benefit: When an Oath member lets the secret sleeping in her chest creep up to their tongue, she finds herself speaking with the tone and demeanor of her co-conspirators. Once per chapter, they can exchange an equal number of social Merits dots for which they both qualify. She can\u2019t gain or lend Court Mantle through this, though Court Goodwill is fair game. Merit ratings revert immediately the next time any beneficiary suffers damage to her Clarity.<br /> <br /> Consequences: Betraying the silence of the Wyrd beckons haunting, accusatory echoes: neither in briars nor slumber shall the infringing party find succor. All Fae beings aware of her former deception gain a bonus equal to the Oathbreaker\u2019s Wyrd rating to all Hedgespinning or Dreamweaving rolls targeting her, if they incorporate damning references to it in their action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Oath of Sharing</b><br /> When any prized property (often a Token, sometimes a creature, turf, or even hostage) is too precious for a single owner to retain it, this Oath cements a sense of joint responsibilities among two or more Lost. Those who pledge may freely establish the length between two changes of custody, as long as the division of time is equal among all members.<br /> <br /> Terms: <i>\u201c</i>Between our hands lies a treasure which none of us may solely lay claim to. As dusk follows dawn, ceaseless and without gripe, we shall take turns using it: and in the case one of us claims its use in vital urgency, promptly shall the other journey to cede it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Beat: The changeling cedes her counterpart another resource she likely could have used herself.<br /> <br /> Willpower: The changeling takes a risk or expends resources to check in on the safety of her counterpart(s).<br /> <br /> Benefit: Upon every transfer of the prized item, each owner transfers bits and pieces of her mystical identity with the others, so much so that it is not always clear which is which. Once per chapter, they can levy this connection to switch an equal number of Physical or Mental Merit dots between each other, provided they both qualify to their prequisites. Merit ratings revert immediately the next time any beneficiary suffers damage to her Clarity.<br /> <br /> Consequences: The broken Oath dredges up the inner divide between the Moon and Sun, relegating the Oathbreaker to either the nocturnal or sunlit hours (as chosen by the ST). During the other half of the day, she feels unwelcome and clumsy in a foreign territory \u2013 a dim mote in the dusk, or a lingering shade in the light. She typically gets the cold shoulder from diurnal/nocturnal creatures, and the Availability of any goods or services she seeks to acquire during that time increases by two.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Oath of Scorn</b><br /> When the necessity of outer decorum or forced cooperation discourage the striking of the Oath of Nemesis or the prospect of a Feud, yet your blood boils and your mood sours at the sight of your favorite rival, this Oath offers you a chance at a more distinguished affrontement: good, old, sweet passive-agression.<br /> <br /> Terms: \u201cYour blood is too foul for me to spill it, your suffering too sweet for an early death to snuff it. With naught but my words and awareness of your flaws, I swear to lay your life to waste in front of your very eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Beat: The changeling gets one or several allies of her foe to publicly denounce a positive opinion formerly held about him.<br /> <br /> Willpower: The changeling verbally tears into an aspect of her enemy\u2019s life in his presence, and walks away unscathed.<br /> <br /> Consequences: If the Oath is broken by an untimely truce or a misguided blow, the Oathbreaker becomes a paper tiger in the eyes of the Wyrd, unready to wield the refined cruelty of either words or wounds. Whenever she intends to cause physical or Clarity damage through deed or Contract, her action only deals bashing damage: to inflict the regular amount of pain, she must spend 1 Glamour, or succeed on a social roll to look suitably menacing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Oath of Adoption</b><br /> With few hard benefits, heavy responsibilities, and vague requirements all too easily violated, this Oath is somewhat of a rarity \u2013 mainly appealing to elder changelings envisioning every interaction through the lens of their potent Wyrd, or to those of the Lost who resent their inability to produce offspring, unable to find in the friendships of a motley the warmth of a parental embrace.<br /> <br /> Terms: \u201cYou walk a path that is your own: but henceforth, you don\u2019t walk alone. You are my ward, foremost recipient of my counsel. May my guidance steer you towards your goal; may my example shield you from my mistakes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Beat: The mentor deliberately chooses to fail a roll, in order to impart her ward a tough life lesson.<br /> <br /> Willpower: The ward acts in a way reflective of her mentor's Needle or Thread, without any coercion from the latter.<br /> <br /> Benefit: As per the Arcadian Dreams Condition (CtL p.333), but reciprocal.<br /> <br /> Consequences: If the ward dies, or if an irrevocable breach of trust separates her from her mentor, the most potent of griefs swallows the Oathbreaker. He acquires a Frailty towards any object or account strongly reminiscent of the other (current or former possessions, depictions, recordings, or even sufficiently heartfelt testimonies of people who met them). The Wyrd always seem to be far harsher towards the mentor, both in detection of infringing acts and in the magnitude of the punishment.<br /> \u200b <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 02-15-2024, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}